module gunbc.integration_concern.emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal

// One row of the integration-concern register. The roster derives the row from this file (module gunbc.integration_concern.roster);
// there is no list to append to. Ported from main's block in gunbc.integration_concern
// at merge 19: main 50c45934852.

import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import std.optional { Absent }
import gunbc.integration_concern { CitesDeclaration, ConcernSighting, IntegrationConcern, Open, RequirementEstablished, SuspectedCapabilityGap, emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal_review }

// THE __GUNBC_INVOKE_EMIT_REFUSED__ REFUSAL FAMILY, STATED IN ONE PLACE. The run-step emitter refuses
// three ways -- the word wall (gunbc_invoke_word_unsafe_poison), the orchestration rejection
// (gunbc_invoke_step_orch_refused_poison), and a target whose module derives no storage path
// (gunbc_run_step_target_unstored_poison) -- and all three collapse their typed refusal into a marker
// STRING in the rendered bytes, which gunbc.generated_artifact_production workflow_body_generated later finds
// with a prefix scan. Each refusal locates itself (the word or the sanitized module_path/decl_name
// follows the marker) and the committed-workflow door is closed while the scan stands, but a refusal
// rendered into anything the scan does not read travels untyped. The honest terminal shape is one
// carrier: every *_invoke job body returns a refusal carrier that string concatenation preserves,
// unwrapped ONCE at gunbc.generated_artifact_emit artifact_generate into ArtifactGenerationRefused --
// at which point all three poisons and the scan are deleted together. P2a (#16467, review 95421)
// filed this instead of building it: the retype is a cross-emitter change of ~140 String-returning job
// bodies, a different change than retyping the roster. The gate scan is the single wall meanwhile, and
// a new refusal sibling must join the one prefix the scan checks.
data emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_run_step_script_for_target"),
    requirement: "a run-step emit that cannot render its target returns a typed, located refusal through the job-body chain, unwrapped once at gunbc.generated_artifact_emit artifact_generate into ArtifactGenerationRefused, rather than rendering a __GUNBC_INVOKE_EMIT_REFUSED__ marker string that the Tier O gate must later find by scanning the committed bytes (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed: every path succeeds fully or fails with a typed, located diagnostic)",
    standing: RequirementEstablished { by: emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal_review },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_invoke_word_unsafe_poison"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_invoke_step_orch_refused_poison"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_run_step_target_unstored_poison"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.generated_artifact_production", decl_name: "workflow_body_generated"),
    ],
  },
  question: "when the *_invoke job bodies return a typed refusal carrier unwrapped once at artifact_generate, delete the three poisons and the workflow_body_generated prefix scan together. Until then the family is mitigatable, stated as such: located markers behind one prefix, the scan the only gate, and any render outside the scan's reach unguarded.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "b45535c5d7f184b7ec9ffb687f7c387705f9b247",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_run_step_target_unstored_poison") },
        tail: [
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_invoke_word_unsafe_poison") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.generated_artifact_production", decl_name: "workflow_body_generated") },
        ],
      },
      account: "P2a added the third sibling (the unstored-target poison beside the word wall and orchestration poisons) and the Tier O prefix scan; dashboard review 95421 on gunb-ai/gunbc#16467 at head b45535c5d7f (Verdict: REQUEST_CHANGES) judged marker-string plus string_contains a fail_closed fork for the Absent arm. The family-wide retype was ruled its own change, not P2a; this row is its trigger. Dashboard review 95484 on the same PR (Verdict: REQUEST_CHANGES) refused the per-character sanitizer that had been duplicated beside the alphabet's home; this row's own citations were the proof (they named the copy by home). It is now deleted: the Absent arm renders through gunbc_invoke_sanitize_word, the family's single character map, so the family keeps ONE sanitizer and this concern tracks only the typed threading.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Open,
}
